<title>SRI LANKA: Aitken Spence up on tourism revival.</title>
<headline>Aitken Spence up on tourism revival.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Aitken Spence &amp; Co Ltd rose 6.28 percent, or 9.75 rupees to 165, in late Friday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The company is seen doing well in 1997, on the back of improved tourist arrivals,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Aitken Spence, one of three blue chip conglomerates listed in Colombo, owns and manages hotels in Sri Lanka and the Maldives.</p>
<p>The government Tourist Board says arrivals in the first quarter of 1997 rose 17 percent, after falling 25 percent in 1996 when separatist rebels bombed the Central Bank and a crowded commuter train.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
